\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx204\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 IN No. I of }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid10959261 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 TH}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 E}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  MUSIC }{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 REVIEW, February, 1940, \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
Otto Erich Deutsch, the distinguished scholar and Schubert biographer, has given a comprehensive account of the history and the adventures of a masterpiece, the riddle of which consists in the fact of its having remained a torso. Unfinished works, general
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 l\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 y, have been cut off by death, as for example Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s }{\i\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Art of Fugue, }{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Mozart\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s }{\i\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Requiem, }{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Bruckner\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s Ninth and Mahler\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s Tenth symphony. But Schubert wrote these two glorious movements in 1822, six years before his early death, and practically all his great mast\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
erpieces of instrumental music were composed afterwards. There cannot be any doubt that he was conscious of the momentous importance of that torso, his greatest achievement until then: why did he abandon it?
\par }\pard \qj \fi345\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx345\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 The answer to this question flashed into my mind\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
, many years ago, when I first set eyes on an appendix to Schubert\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s manuscript, a sketch of a scherzo, unmistakably destined to be the third move\-
ment of the symphony in B minor, and mentioned also by O. E. Deutsch in his essay. This sketch was published\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 in the editor\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s commentary on the complete edition of Schubert
\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s works, and it rules out once and for all the absurd idea of the symphony having been intended to consist of only two movements. When I added it as a supplement in a new miniature score, publ\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 i
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 shed in 1923 by the Vienna Philharmonic Edition, I was convinced no further commentary would be required, since to my mind that sketch itself reveals the solution of the riddle.
\par }\pard \qj \fi345\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx351\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10959261 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 The sketch comprises a complete draft of the scherzo and the first part of a t
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
rio. One page of a full score, containing the first nine bars, gives a definite impression of its whole character. I cannot imagine a musician reading the sketch who would not feel amazed by the emptiness of this unfortunate piece of music, even apart fro
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 m\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  its context. But comparing it with the loftiness and the lavish wealth of that glorious }{\i\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 allegro}{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  and that heavenly }{\i\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 andante}{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid1075487\charrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 ,}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid12859582 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 one is unable to conceive how anything as poor, as narrow, as sterile  could possibly grow out of the same soil. This is a riddle, n\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 o doubt!}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid12859582 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 But one can, find examples of a similar kind among the works of  the greatest masters, and Schubert was still on the threshold of}{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid12859582 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
his mastery when he wrote that music. A temporary intermission of creative power, a sudden weakness of the inventive \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
imagination, is a phenomenon well known to the artist. There has been no musician, no poet in the world, who has not known the depressing experience at one time or another of the mysterious, undefinable motor of his invention stopping suddenly. It comes, 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 a\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 nd it passes, like an illness. Schubert\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s sketch gives in every detail a clinical aspect of that illness. 
\par }\pard \qj \fi351\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx351\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10959261 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid12859582 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 It opens with a theme of eight bars, the second half of which}{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261\charrsid12859582 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 is nothing but a sequence:}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid10959261 
\par }{\b\fs20\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid198126\charrsid198126 
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 (a)      Allegro
